Vendored from libs.suckless.org/libgrapheme (git://git.suckless.org/libgrapheme).
Unicode 17.0.0 grapheme-cluster + line/word/sentence/case/bidi tables.
ISC-licensed.

Files:
  *.c                  — source files (8 .c, ~4500 LoC)
  util.h               — internal API
  grapheme.h           — public API
  *_data.h             — pre-generated Unicode tables
                         (originally gen/X.h; renamed to *_data.h to avoid
                          name collision with src/X.c after flattening)
  gen_types.h          — shared types for the data tables
                         (originally gen/types.h)
  LICENSE.txt          — ISC

Build pre-step (already done at vendoring time): the upstream build runs
gen/X (compiled C programs) against data/*.txt to produce gen/X.h tables.
The output of that step is what's vendored here.

Path-rewriting done at vendor time:
  #include "../gen/X.h"   → #include "X_data.h"
  #include "../grapheme.h" → #include "grapheme.h"
  #include "types.h"      → #include "gen_types.h"

After patch-bash-loadables.sh flattening:
  builtins/_libgrapheme_*.{c,h}  for everything

Loadables that need libgrapheme include:
  #include "_libgrapheme_grapheme.h"

API entry points (see grapheme.h):
  grapheme_next_character_break_utf8()  — for cell-width / cursor positioning
  grapheme_decode_utf8() / grapheme_encode_utf8()
  grapheme_next_line_break_utf8()       — for word-wrap
